ix of stored contexts, but handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation sends each remote destination the triggering message context instead of that released item's stored context, whereas local completion uses the stored context. No overlapping legal history or endpoint has been executed. An initially suspicious absence of an observer check in heartbeat response consumption is insufficient: broadcastHeartbeatMessageWithHint sends nonzero contexts only to voters. Peer.Handle also rejects responses from unknown members, and candidate vote handling rejects observers.\",\n        \"remaining\": [\n          \"Complete core_overview and partial Behavior/Fact map after tracing startup/reconstruction, membership application ownership, update/application completion and timeout/retry paths; current reading is not a usable-map declaration.\",\n          \"Trace production of distinct overlapping forwarded ReadIndex contexts, batching/serialization, and all resend/timeout paths to determine whether the remote-context difference can occur in one legal history and which precise correlation responsibility applies.\",\n          \"Trace log.tryCommit, history conflict handling and persistent restart loading rather than relying on caller names or comments for their guarantees.\",\n          \"Determine applicable caller and fault contracts from captured interfaces/documents; the listed sources are implementation observations, not a substituted normative specification.\"\n        ],\n        \"understanding\": \"updated\",\n        \"rationale\": \"This preserves both core relationships and the connection between authority, support eligibility and pending work without presuming a finding. The read-response discrepancy has a concrete producer/consumer distinction and warrants source investigation before execution. Broad observer support injection would bypass the actual producer and is not currently justified. No formal Candidate, obligation or Evidence is asserted.\",\n        \"question_updates\": {}\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pending_work\": [],\n  \"current\": {\n    \"phase\": \"executed\",\n    \"operation_id\": \"6895c4584f3f4cf0a6b93d1ad5de78c6\",\n    \"action\": \"research\"\n  },\n  \"latest_decision\": {\n    \"operation_id\": \"6895c4584f3f4cf0a6b93d1ad5de78c6\",\n    \"action\": \"research\",\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"selections\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"operation_id\": \"6895c4584f3f4cf0a6b93d1ad5de78c6\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"stop\": {},\n  \"stop_reason\": \"Not started\",\n  \"explorations\": [],\n  \"review_issues\": [],\n  \"run_id\": \"3ae5e70d2b544c26a3747e18c60be964\",\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"47d7cd7051cf4c99ae1ff19253d9659d\",\n  \"elapsed_seconds\": 216.1080122730018,\n  \"source_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run/agent-source\",\n  \"draft_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run/draft\",\n  \"state_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run/state.json\",\n  \"product_schemas\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run/product-schemas.json\",\n  \"submission_schema\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run/submission.schema.json\",\n  \"method_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run/audit-method.md\",\n  \"directed_question\": null,\n  \"tools\": {\n    \"agent\": \"codex-cli 0.155.0-alpha.16\",\n    \"implementation\": \"go version go1.23.5 linux/amd64\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"go_module\",\n    \"harness_kind\": \"go_test\",\n    \"default_execution_package\": \".\",\n    \"harness_filename\": \"assurance_generated_test.go\",\n    \"instructions\": \"Use TestAssurance-prefixed Go tests in the selected lo