s=['B-replicate','B-read-confirm','B-persistence','B-apply'],fact_ids=['F-committed','F-read-release'],source_ids=['S-core-commit','S-log-guards','S-engine-order','S-rsm-entry','S-read-entry']),context=dict(explanation='Ticks initiate elections for eligible regular members; log freshness and one-vote rules qualify support. Candidate votes are deduplicated; peer admission excludes unknown response senders and candidate handling excludes observers. Term transitions and role resets discard pending read support, votes and remote progress. Higher-term vote suppression under a recent known leader is conditional on CheckQuorum. Transfer catches up an eligible target and invokes the ordinary election path; loss of quorum or removal can demote. Restart restores history but not leadership.',behavior_ids=['B-authority','B-transfer','B-recovery'],fact_ids=['F-authority'],source_ids=['S-term-election','S-vote-response','S-peer-admission','S-ticks','S-transfer','S-start']),connection=dict(explanation='New leaders retain prior log decisions but reset replication accounting, scan pending configuration work and append a current-term noop. Current-term commitment gates multi-node read confirmation. Committed-but-unapplied work blocks campaigning because it can change the quorum; RSM membership application updates raft under raftMu. Snapshot recovery restores state before remotes are reconstituted. Old-term replies are rejected; authority reset clears pending read contexts; client batches independently await correlated ready state and applied index or timeout.',behavior_ids=['B-authority','B-membership','B-recovery','B-read-client','B-read-confirm','B-apply'],fact_ids=['F-authority','F-committed','F-read-release'],source_ids=['S-core-commit','S-term-election','S-rsm-config','S-node-apply','S-rsm-recover','S-read-consumer']),open_details=['Remote read-prefix responses use triggering context rather than each released context; legal overlap and responsibility need a fixed investigation.'