 the producer rules out arbitrary observer acknowledgements; a bounded overlapping history can now discriminate encoding behavior more directly than a whole-cluster timing test.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',source_ids=['S-read-response','S-read-aggregation','S-read-batch','S-read-consumer','S-read-contract','S-forward-read'],participants=['Leader','Forwarding follower or observer','Voting heartbeat responder'],objects=['Pending readStatus prefix','ReadIndexResp','ReadyToRead'],contexts=['Stable term and voting membership after a current-term entry is committed','Distinct nonzero contexts admitted before confirmation'],event_paths=['Node read batches -> Peer.ReadIndex -> follower forwarding -> leader pending queue -> later contextual heartbeat confirmation -> prefix response emission -> follower ReadyToRead'],activity_classes=['A1'],behavior_ids=['B-read-confirm','B-read-receive'],fact_ids=['F-read-release'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-read-client':'Establishes independently pending context batches and exact-context completion consumer.','B-authority':'Explains term qualification and reset of pending support.','B-replicate':'Establishes current-term committed entry prerequisite.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Single outstanding forwarded request has the same stored and triggering context.','Local prefix completion uses each stored context.','Earlier heartbeat response can complete the earlier request first; schedule must preserve the overlapping prefix.','Timeout notification is supported, so non-completion alone supplies no general deadline violation.'],unknowns=['Whether transport batching or internal adaptation imposes additional ordering before a chosen Peer-level controlled history.','Exact scoped responsibility and independent oracle for remote correlation, separated from any automatic-progress claim.'],priority=2)\nsubmission=dict(action='continue',rationale='Record usable core map and select the concrete remote read-context discrepancy without presuming violation; fixed construction will follow entry/lifecycle and transport adaptation inspection.',map_path='map.json',sources=sources,question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S-log-guards','S-read-batch','S-read-timeout','S-rsm-recover','S-rsm-config'],answered='Log commitment enforces current-term counting and committed-prefix immutability. RSM application owns membership acceptance and calls raft under node locking; snapshot recovery restores remotes after state recovery. Normal read batching creates distinct contexts on successive steps while previous batches remain pending; timeout collection does not resend ReadIndex. These answers are incorporated into the initial map.',remaining=q['unknowns'],understanding='updated',rationale='Resolves prior backbone gaps and the admission-overlap premise through actual callers without equating source observations to executed evidence.'))\njson.dump(submission,open('submission-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_map.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission submission-map.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
