.','Storage backend crash behavior, snapshot transfer failure variants, session completion and concurrent reconfiguration details remain open.'])\nm=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Dragonboat Go module: NodeHost/node engine, internal raft, RSM, persistence and transport integration; application implementations remain caller-supplied but their in-repository adapters remain in scope.',protocol_contexts=['Independent clusterID/nodeID instances with term/log and voting membership.'],external_interfaces=['NodeHost ReadIndex/ReadLocalNode','Peer message/update API'],source_ids=['S-read-contract','S-launch','S-engine-order']),activities=activities,behaviors=bs,facts=facts,core_overview=overview,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='raft.handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-read-confirm','B-read-receive'],reason='Does coalesced confirmation preserve each released remote request context?',source_ids=['S-read-response','S-read-aggregation'],high_consequence=False),dict(entry_point='engine.SaveRaftState backend and snapshot transport',disposition='deferred',reason='What concrete backend and transport failure contracts preserve recovered support?',source_ids=['S-engine-order','S-replay'],high_consequence=True)])\njson.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='When a later heartbeat confirms a prefix containing multiple forwarded ReadIndex requests, does the leader preserve each released request context in its response to that requester?',importance='A mismatched response context may strand an otherwise confirmed read batch until timeout. No stale-read safety violation or global progress failure is asserted.',trigger_rationale='confirm returns records with distinct stored contexts and destinations, but the remote branch encodes the same triggering heartbeat context for every record; the local branch uses each record context. Normal node steps admit fresh batches without awaiting prior completion. Source review of the producer rules out arbitrary observer acknowledgements; a bounded overlapping history can now discriminate encoding behavior more directly than a whole-cluster timing test.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',source_ids=['S-read-response','S-read-aggregation','S-read-batch','S-read-consumer','S-read-contract','S-forward-read'],participants=['Leader','Forwarding follower or observer','Voting heartbeat responder'],objects=['Pending readStatus prefix','ReadIndexResp','ReadyToRead'],contexts=['Stable term and voting membership after a current-term entry is committed','Distinct nonzero contexts admitted before confirmation'],event_paths=['Node read batches -> Peer.ReadIndex -> follower forwarding -> leader pending queue -> later contextual heartbeat confirmation -> prefix response emission -> follower ReadyToRead'],activity_classes=['A1'],behavior_ids=['B-read-confirm','B-read-receive'],fact_ids=['F-read-release'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-read-client':'Establishes independently pending context batches and exact-context completion consumer.','B-authority':'Explains term qualification and reset of pending support.','B-replicate':'Establishes current-term committed entry prerequisite.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Single outstanding forwarded request has the same stored and triggering context.','Local prefix completion uses each stored context.','Earlier heartbeat response can complete the earlier request first; schedule must preserve the overlapping prefix.','Timeout notification is supported, so non-completion alone supplies no general deadline violation.'],unknowns=['Whether transport batching or internal adaptation imposes additional ordering before a chosen Peer-level controlled history.','Exact scoped responsibility and independent oracle for remote correlation, separated from any automatic-progress claim.'],priority=2)\nsubmission=dict(action='continue',rationale='Record usable core map and select the concrete remote read-context discrepancy without presuming violation; fixed construction will follow entry/lifecycle and transport adaptation inspection.',map_path='map.json',sources=sources,question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S-log-guards','S-read-batch','S-read-timeout','S-rsm-recover','S-rsm-config'],answered='Log commitment enforces current-term counting and committed-prefix immutability. RSM application owns membership acceptance and calls raft under node locking; snapshot recovery restores remotes after state recovery. Normal read batching creates distinct contexts on successive steps while previous batches remain pending; timeout collection does not resend ReadIndex. These answers are incorporated into the initial map.',remaining=q['unknowns'],understanding='updated',rationale='Resolves prior backbone gaps and the admission-overlap premise through actual callers without equating source observations to executed evidence.'))\njson.dump(submission,open('submission-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_map.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission submission-map.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": false, \"run_id\": \"3ae5e70d2b544c26a3747e18c60be964\", \"audit_spec_version\": 0, \"elapsed_seconds\": 216.1080122730018, \"diagnostics\": [{\"details\": {}, \"code\": \"core_overview\", \"category\": \"semantic\", \"task\": \"\", \"candidate_version\": 0, \"object_ids\": [], \"paths\": [\"/core_overview/connection/source_ids\"], \"material_ids\": [], \"message\": \"Cite the referenced Behavior and Fact sources; labels alone do not explain a path\", \"allowed\": [\"read\", \"semantic_revision\"]}, {\"detail